<h1>simple path</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="path.html"><em>path</em></a> that repeats no <a href="vertex.html"><em>vertex</em></a>, except that the first and last may be the same vertex.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="hamiltonianPath.html"><em>Hamiltonian path</em></a>, <a href="cycle.html"><em>cycle</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
enumerate <a href="allSimplePaths.html"><em>all simple paths</em></a> between two vertices.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
In August 2017 the definition changed to allow the first and last vertex to be the same, consistent with Knuth  <a href="../terms.html#Knuth98">[Knuth98, 1:363]</a>.  Before, the definition was "A path that repeats no vertex."</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

